# rule-presence.manifest -- load-bearing rule sentences that MUST stay present in the
# repo tree. Consumed by validate-rule-presence.sh (wired into scripts/ci/run-all.sh).
#
# Format: one row per registered sentence, TAB-separated:
#     <repo-relative-file><TAB><canonical rule sentence>
# Lines beginning with '#' and blank lines are ignored.
#
# Normalization -- the registered sentence is normalized as one line; the target file
# is normalized PARAGRAPH-LOCALLY (one blank-line-delimited block at a time):
#   1. join soft-wrapped lines WITHIN a paragraph into one logical line (every run of
#      whitespace, soft-wrap newlines included, becomes a single space) -- paragraph
#      breaks are NOT bridged, so a sentence split by an inserted paragraph break stops
#      matching. A paragraph break is any line with no non-whitespace content: a truly
#      empty line OR a line holding only spaces/tabs (Markdown treats both the same);
#   2. collapse remaining whitespace runs to a single space;
#   3. strip leading/trailing whitespace;
#   4. drop a single trailing '.' or ':';
#   5. case-sensitive otherwise.
# The check PASSES for a row when its normalized sentence is a substring of some
# normalized paragraph of the target file. A missing target file or an empty manifest
# is a failure.
#
# Registration rules:
#   - Register only text that lives in a file BODY, or in a frontmatter line that no
#     install transform rewrites. NEVER register a 'tools:' / 'disallowedTools:' /
#     'tier:' / 'model:' value -- install-opencode.sh:199-236 rewrites exactly those.
#   - Do not register a line containing ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}: install-opencode.sh
#     rewrites that placeholder to a literal path in agent/skill/command files.
#   - Every registered sentence must additionally survive the OpenCode agent transform
#     (validate-rule-presence.sh --post-install <DEST>); skills/commands are copied
#     verbatim so only the agent frontmatter transform is exercised.
#
# Reword rule: if a registered sentence is legitimately reworded in a source file
# (e.g. retro-improve's <=3-sentence-per-file cap), its manifest row is updated in the
# SAME commit as the source edit -- never left stale, never deleted to dodge the check.
#
# Coverage: every skills/*/SKILL.md (all 13 dirs) is represented. The 12 non-canonical
# skill dirs each register their full anti-hallucination POINTER SENTENCE ("All factual
# output follows the anti-hallucination skill: ..."). The 13th dir, anti-hallucination/
# itself, carries no pointer, so it registers its canonical-source line instead ("This is
# the one place the rule is stated in full"). backend-design/ and premortem/ ADDITIONALLY
# register "User instructions always override this skill" -- a second load-bearing line in
# those two files; those rows are extra coverage, never a substitute for the pointer row.
# Reference-file and agent rules follow below.
#
# Belt-and-braces gap this closes: validate-skills.sh:42 only greps each SKILL.md for the
# bare token 'anti-hallucination' anywhere in the file, so the full pointer SENTENCE (and
# its exact wording) is otherwise unprotected -- gutting a pointer down to a bare token
# leaves validate-skills.sh green. Registering the sentence here pins it. This holds only
# while every pointer-bearing SKILL.md has its sentence row below; keep the two in sync.
#
# --post-install constraint: every row path below MUST live under 'plugins/sefi-core/'.
# --post-install strips exactly that prefix to resolve rows against the tree
# install-opencode.sh writes; a row outside that prefix is rejected (exit 1), never
# guessed. A future row for a repo file outside plugins/sefi-core/ needs the resolver
# taught that path first.
#
# Deviations from state/plan-astral-adoption.md Phase 1 step 1, each verified against the
# named file at build time (the plan text was written before these files were re-read):
#   - "consume-before-act" is NOT a human-checkpoint.md rule; it lives in
#     loop-discipline.md:28 (the "four predecessor-earned rules" sentence, registered
#     below against loop-discipline.md).
#   - loop-discipline.md contains NO "five-move loop" sentence; the load-bearing loop
#     rules registered instead are its stop-conditions rule and its
#     SKIP/degrade/escalate rule (loop-discipline.md:9-13).
#   - the envelope / check-handoff.sh-before-dispatch rule is NOT in scope-boundary.md;
#     it lives in sefi-orchestration/SKILL.md:49,58,67,69 and is registered below
#     against that file ("Write the handoff as an envelope ...", "A blocked envelope is
#     fixed and re-checked, never dispatched anyway"). scope-boundary.md carries the
#     related but distinct "belongs to another agent" / "not permission" rules, also
#     registered below.
plugins/sefi-core/skills/loop-engineering/SKILL.md	All factual output follows the anti-hallucination skill: cite or mark UNKNOWN, never guess
plugins/sefi-core/skills/memory-protocol/SKILL.md	All factual output follows the anti-hallucination skill: cite or mark UNKNOWN, never guess
plugins/sefi-core/skills/retro-improve/SKILL.md	All factual output follows the anti-hallucination skill: cite or mark UNKNOWN, never guess
